00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:37.670
and you'll have all the ice cream you can eat.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:38.470
Me too?

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.590
Dottie, now you know what I said.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.650
And you were absolutely right.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.070
This ought to be a good one.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:48.050
I really was going to bring my chocolate fudge and enter it.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:50.020
But I knew I'd never get away with it.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:50.930
Not with you.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.010
You're just too smart for me, Larry.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.190
So you came down to tell me that, right?

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.150
Uh-huh. It's only fair.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.000
She's my idol. Why can't I think of things like that?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:03.320
All right, Shorty. Go stand in the corner till we're through.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.200
And then you can join us for ice cream.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.200
Yes, sir.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:10.720
All right, let's get this rolling, Larry.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.760
Just watching him makes me lose my appetite.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.760
Okay, Sheriff.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.650
To begin with, we had three prime suspects.

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:22.050
Mr. Reese, who had the only key to the pig pen machinery.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:26.910
Uh-huh. Dirty badge, dirty crook. It's for old bloodhound thingin'.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:30.000
Mr. Glutt, who was offering a lot of money to...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.980
by Sweet Pea and Mr. Cleek,

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:33.820
who is playing a part for his own reasons.

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:35.440
Told ya, told ya!

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:37.080
The butler done it.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:39.820
Now you wait just one minute, Larry.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.370
I never touched Sweet Pea.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.230
I know how much you love that animal.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.110
I believe you, Mr. Reese.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:46.340
So do we.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:48.330
We know you didn't do it, Mr. Reese.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.310
Then you must also know

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.550
that I would never stoop to pig napping.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.070
Nor would I associate with a man who did.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:58.470
Mmm, well said, Cleek.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:00.000
and more sandwiches.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.000
Quickly!

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.860
I feel a hunger pang coming on.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:05.860
Immediately, sir.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.610
We also know that Mr. Glutt wasn't the pig-napper.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.610
Now, hold it right there, Larry. Those are the only suspects we got.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:18.880
Not quite, Sheriff. The real criminal waited until Sally and Mr. Reese left.

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:23.040
Then he climbed the ferris wheel and hooked a rope to the removable end of the pig pen.

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.200
Then he climbed down and started it up.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.760
Once there was enough room for Sweet Pea to get out,

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.200
the machine was stopped.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:37.040
That's how the strands of hemp got on the ferris wheel.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.580
Pepper thought they were blonde hair.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.380
But when I got them under the microscope...

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:41.380
Dottie!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.080
Oops.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.580
Well, let's suppose it all happened that way.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.430
How'd the animal get down?

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:49.110
I still say pigs can't fly.

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:50.850
This one didn't have to.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.350
The pig knapper was pretty clever.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:57.110
He sprinkled kernels of corn on a roller conveyor,

00:20:57.110 --> 00:21:00.000
lifted it to the pan, and Sweet Pea did the rest.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.400
Hey, Larry, where is Sweet Pea?

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.330
Right where Mr. Clay left him, Sally.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.160
The ice cream shack.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:12.270
For hours, that's all I needed.

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:16.270
And I'd have sold that porker to Mr. Glutt for $75,000.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:19.270
Well, you'll have plenty of time to think about that. Let's go.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:21.270
Sweet Pea!

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:24.270
Young lady, I'll make you one final offer.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:28.150
$100,000, and not a penny more.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:30.000
Hoo-hee!

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:32.910
One hundred thousand smackers for a pig!

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:35.880
No, sir! I'll never sell sweet pea!

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:38.760
Ooh, that girl is making a mighty big mistake!

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:41.160
Ain't nobody worth a hundred thousand!

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.020
Well, how about Dottie?

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:45.500
Dottie?! Don't be ridiculous!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.000
When you talk about Dott--

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.340
A hundred thousand dollars?

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.360
Hmm...

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:52.950
Well now, you gotta understand...

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.640
Is that in cash?

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.680
I mean, a dog has gotta think about his future!
